hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2688","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Ja'far al-Raqqqi, narrated to us 'Ubaydullah—meaning ibn 'Amr al-Raqqqi—on the authority of Zayd—who is ibn Abi Unaysah—on the authority of Yahya ibn al-Husayn al-Ahmasiy, on the authority of Umm al-Husayn, his grandmother, who said:\n\n\I performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) during the Farewell Pilgrimage. I saw Usamah ibn Zayd and Bilal. One of them was leading the camel by its halter"," while the other was raising his garment to shield him from the heat until they stoned the Jamrah of 'Aqabah.\""\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""
